==Battleground==
*1 [[Zamelle]] spawns as the boss after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 21.67 seconds<sup>650f</sup>, delay 50~100 seconds<sup>1,500f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 38.33 seconds<sup>1,150f</sup>, delay 50~100 seconds<sup>1,500f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 33.33~66.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~2,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 96% HP:
**8 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 92% HP:
**8 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 88% HP:
**8 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The actual threat of the stage is the barrages of Brollows that spawn on base hit, it is important to carefully damage the base after the Zamelle to avoid spawning multiple waves which can result in almost instant death without either a huge amount of meatshields or [[Surge Attack|Surge attackers]].

It is also recommended to use [[Holy Blast]], as the default Cat Cannon will cause the Brollow hordes to rebound, while Holy Blast both ignores the Brollows and does huge damage against the Zombies. [[Iron Wall]]/[[Slow Beam]] is also a decent choice for stopping the Brollows as they don't reset the Brollows' backswing and can slow them down. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] can finish off Zamelle when the Brollows are fully cleared out.

Anti-Floating tank units such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus]] or [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] can help stop the wave sooner.

==Trivia==
*50 Degrees Hotter may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Fifty Shades Darker|Fifty Shades Darker]]'', an erotic romance novel whose movie adaptation was released not long after the stage was added to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]].
*50 Degrees Hotter's Japanese name, World of Plus 50 Degrees, is a reference to either the book ''[https://www.amazon.co.jp/%E3%83%9E%E3%82%A4%E3%83%8A%E3%82%B9%EF%BC%95%EF%BC%90%E2%84%83%E3%81%AE%E4%B8%96%E7%95%8C-%E8%A7%92%E5%B7%9D%E3%82%BD%E3%83%95%E3%82%A3%E3%82%A2%E6%96%87%E5%BA%AB-%E7%B1%B3%E5%8E%9F-%E4%B8%87%E9%87%8C-ebook/dp/B00CPEB8MS Minus 50℃ no Sekai]'' (World of Minus 50°C), or to [https://www.greenland.co.jp/park/attraction/iceworld/ Ice World: World of Minus 30 Degrees], an attraction at Japanese amusement parks such as Cosmo World and Kijima Kogen Park. Since the stage is found in [[Mouseyland]], the latter is more likely.

